WEBVTT

00:00:07.950 --> 00:00:13.450
"To make laugh"

00:00:16.290 --> 00:00:18.910
I'm thinking of becoming a nun.

00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:26.830
Since we've been living together a while,
I've learned how to decipher you, Miss Minare.

00:00:26.830 --> 00:00:30.330
I can tell if you're saying something serious
or if you're going to change your mind

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:31.870
about it in a day or two.

00:00:31.870 --> 00:00:36.410
It's not like that, Mizuho.
I'm always serious when I say it.

00:00:36.410 --> 00:00:38.450
You know, how since the dawn of history...

00:00:38.450 --> 00:00:43.540
Humans have killed animals, torn down forests,
and contaminated rivers to expand their habitat?

00:00:43.540 --> 00:00:46.950
But the moment we feel some level of ease
in our lives, that's when we realize

00:00:46.950 --> 00:00:50.700
how terribly we've been treating Mother Nature.

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:52.620
I'm in that exact headspace now.

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:56.580
I've lived my life too selfishly without
thinking about the suffering of others.

00:00:56.580 --> 00:00:58.120
I know I'm the one barging in on your life,

00:00:58.120 --> 00:01:01.080
but I often get stricken with grief
while living with you, Mizuho.

00:01:01.080 --> 00:01:02.000
But why?

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:05.330
No matter how tired you are, you change
the water in the turtles' tank twice a week.

00:01:05.330 --> 00:01:08.790
You always plate the ready-made food
so nicely and make me tea all the time.

00:01:08.790 --> 00:01:10.750
You're so attentive and generous.

00:01:10.750 --> 00:01:11.750
Oh...

00:01:11.750 --> 00:01:16.700
Meanwhile, I serve customers extremely
diluted instant coffee as barley tea,

00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:20.330
I have ten socks that can't be
paired up in my dresser,

00:01:20.330 --> 00:01:23.660
when I borrowed the <i>Onna Taikoki</i>
DVD from my friend,

00:01:23.660 --> 00:01:27.160
I accidentally returned it
with <i>Shogun's Sadism </i>instead!

00:01:27.160 --> 00:01:29.250
And the list goes on and on!

00:01:29.250 --> 00:01:32.950
That's why I've decided to live the rest
of my life praying for the peace of others.

00:01:32.950 --> 00:01:35.660
When I did some research, I saw listings for
a one-day nun experience and nun role-play

00:01:35.660 --> 00:01:37.790
being offered in Sapporo,
so I'm going to go check it out!

00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:45.000
Miss Minare, I've been told
the same thing ever since I was small.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:48.790
"You're so nice." "You're so helpful."
"You're so proper."

00:01:48.790 --> 00:01:52.750
But it's like I don't have any
other strong points besides those.

00:01:52.750 --> 00:01:56.950
Even if I can take care of others, it's not
like I can make things happen by myself.

00:01:56.950 --> 00:02:00.580
I really like you, Miss Minare.
You're my inspiration.

00:02:00.580 --> 00:02:05.080
I get nervous watching you, but you're
someone who has everything I don't have!

00:02:05.080 --> 00:02:09.120
You're like the crystallized form
of inexplicable life energy!

00:02:09.120 --> 00:02:12.450
I don't expect you to be sensitive
or considerate at all!

00:02:12.450 --> 00:02:13.830
Mizuho...

00:02:13.830 --> 00:02:15.750
All right! I change my mind
about becoming a nun.

00:02:15.750 --> 00:02:17.200
I'll go through a sex change and make her happy!

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:18.950
"END OF PLAY"
I'll go through a sex change and make her happy!

00:03:49.830 --> 00:03:50.950
Good night!

00:03:50.950 --> 00:03:51.790
"Episode 8: I Can't Tell You Over the Phone"
Good night!

00:03:51.790 --> 00:03:54.700
"Episode 8: I Can't Tell You Over the Phone"
Have a good night!

00:03:55.790 --> 00:03:57.750
Oh, Nakahara!

00:03:57.750 --> 00:03:59.160
Crap!

00:04:00.410 --> 00:04:02.410
Mr...

00:04:02.410 --> 00:04:03.410
Mr. Takarada...

00:04:03.410 --> 00:04:06.830
"Crap!" Is that what I just heard? Really?

00:04:06.830 --> 00:04:10.330
Well, anyway, I wanted to surprise you,
so that went well.

00:04:10.330 --> 00:04:12.950
I'm just so happy to be back before winter.

00:04:12.950 --> 00:04:17.040
Miss Makie, it's been a while.
You've been such a savior helping us out!

00:04:17.040 --> 00:04:19.870
Oh, please. I didn't do much at all.

00:04:19.870 --> 00:04:22.330
Anyway, who was that who just left? A demon?

00:04:22.330 --> 00:04:26.290
She's one of the mighty crew members
who supported Voyager through its crisis!

00:04:26.290 --> 00:04:28.950
But more importantly, who's this gentleman here?

00:04:29.950 --> 00:04:32.750
You must be Mr. Chuya Nakahara.

00:04:32.750 --> 00:04:34.950
Huh? Yes, that's me.

00:04:35.750 --> 00:04:38.290
I'd like to take this moment to
apologize for the inconveniences

00:04:38.290 --> 00:04:41.540
I caused you due to my carelessness.

00:04:41.540 --> 00:04:42.580
Huh?

00:04:42.580 --> 00:04:44.750
Oh, then you must be...

00:04:44.750 --> 00:04:46.580
Huh? Whoa...

00:04:50.540 --> 00:04:52.040
Makie...

00:04:52.040 --> 00:04:55.250
Go home before you become a further nuisance.

00:04:58.250 --> 00:04:59.620
Minare.

00:04:59.620 --> 00:05:02.000
Just face it already.

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:05.080
We'll end up doing an unedited
live broadcast if you keep this up.

00:05:05.080 --> 00:05:08.660
That's something I want to avoid at all costs...
But dammit, you gotta be kidding me!

00:05:08.660 --> 00:05:13.870
This is what happens when you don't think of
an idea yourself and can't accept anyone else's.

00:05:13.870 --> 00:05:18.790
Since it's broadcast day, I just chose
something from my stock of ideas.

00:05:18.790 --> 00:05:22.700
When there's no time to go do street interviews,
go on location, or do any groundwork,

00:05:22.700 --> 00:05:24.450
we automatically resort to this.

00:05:24.450 --> 00:05:26.500
A segment where you fight with
a family member over the phone

00:05:26.500 --> 00:05:29.200
and have the listeners judge who's right.

00:05:29.200 --> 00:05:31.160
That's all we've got.

00:05:31.160 --> 00:05:32.830
Sorry.

00:05:32.830 --> 00:05:35.370
I'm actually looking forward to this.

00:05:35.370 --> 00:05:37.580
I really wasn't thinking at all.

00:05:37.580 --> 00:05:41.750
When I think about it, this was
the last thing I wanted to do.

00:05:41.750 --> 00:05:44.700
Agh... Dammit!

00:05:44.700 --> 00:05:45.540
Hello.

00:05:45.540 --> 00:05:48.290
Hello? Dad? It's Minare.

00:05:48.290 --> 00:05:49.790
Yeah, I know it's late, sorry.

00:05:49.790 --> 00:05:51.160
So, actually...

00:05:51.160 --> 00:05:55.500
I don't like my name,
so can I change it to Mirei?

00:05:55.500 --> 00:05:56.370
What?

00:05:56.370 --> 00:05:59.700
First off, what is "Minare"?
What language is that, anyway?

00:05:59.700 --> 00:06:02.870
I don't even know what it means,
and it doesn't have a good ring to it.

00:06:02.870 --> 00:06:05.290
My name seriously bothers me.

00:06:05.290 --> 00:06:06.750
--We're going to have the listeners
give their opinion on this subject?

00:06:06.750 --> 00:06:08.370
--You're calling me this
late at night about that?
--We're going to have the listeners
give their opinion on this subject?

00:06:08.370 --> 00:06:09.700
--You're calling me this
late at night about that?
--Maybe she could get
a stage name out of this.

00:06:09.700 --> 00:06:11.120
--Maybe she could get
a stage name out of this.

00:06:11.120 --> 00:06:14.000
Sixty percent of our personalities
go by their stage name.

00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:17.000
The origin of your name? Let's see...

00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:20.540
It was two days after you were born.

00:06:20.540 --> 00:06:23.950
I went to the bookstore to pick up
a copy of a baby names book.

00:06:23.950 --> 00:06:26.700
Really? You actually did something parent-like?

00:06:26.700 --> 00:06:31.410
Then I drifted into the magazine section,
since I couldn't find a good book.

00:06:32.580 --> 00:06:33.830
"Beautiful Mature Women
Celebrities Treasured Photos"

00:06:33.830 --> 00:06:35.830
"Mi Nare"

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:39.200
If that's true, I'm going to
cut all ties with you.

00:06:39.200 --> 00:06:41.540
You saw through that one, huh?

00:06:41.540 --> 00:06:46.000
I said I'd cut ties if that were true.
Which I think is totally possible.

00:06:46.000 --> 00:06:48.540
All right. I'll tell you the truth.

00:06:48.540 --> 00:06:52.290
This was something I wanted to take to my grave.

00:06:52.290 --> 00:06:56.950
When Yui was pregnant with you,
I had three lovers.

00:06:56.950 --> 00:06:59.540
Dad, you can't joke
about that kind of stuff.

00:06:59.540 --> 00:07:03.040
Don't worry. By the time you were born,
I ended it with all of them.

00:07:03.040 --> 00:07:05.790
Of course you did!
But that still doesn't make it okay!

00:07:05.790 --> 00:07:09.040
Well, listen. When I had
the break-up talks with them...

00:07:09.040 --> 00:07:12.700
The youngest one told me this:

00:07:12.700 --> 00:07:15.540
I'm backing out because I love you, Mako.

00:07:15.540 --> 00:07:21.750
But from now on, I want you to remember me
every day just for a few seconds.

00:07:21.750 --> 00:07:28.200
So... When your daughter's born,
maybe you could name her after me.

00:07:29.080 --> 00:07:31.580
I see, so that woman's name was "Minare"--

00:07:31.580 --> 00:07:32.330
No, it was "Natsuko."

00:07:32.330 --> 00:07:33.580
Oh, come on!

00:07:33.580 --> 00:07:37.540
Well, I wish this story were as simple as that.

00:07:37.540 --> 00:07:41.120
But good grief, why do women
have to be like this?

00:07:41.120 --> 00:07:43.080
I'm not trying to be difficult,

00:07:43.080 --> 00:07:45.700
and I'm not interested in
destroying other people's families.

00:07:45.700 --> 00:07:48.620
But maybe in lieu of all that, Mr. Makoto...

00:07:48.620 --> 00:07:50.290
"Michiru"

00:07:51.750 --> 00:07:56.080
If your child is a girl, name her after me.

00:07:56.080 --> 00:08:00.000
Well, if you say no,
I've got some other ideas for you.

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:01.790
"Reiko"

00:08:01.790 --> 00:08:04.250
"Yui Koda"
Mr. Koda, you have an adorable girl now!

00:08:04.660 --> 00:08:05.160
"Open and close the door quietly."

00:08:05.160 --> 00:08:08.000
"Open and close the door quietly."
She looks just like you when you were younger.

00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:10.290
Please name your daughter.

00:08:11.200 --> 00:08:12.700
Um...

00:08:12.700 --> 00:08:14.120
"Michiru Natsuko Reiko"

00:08:14.120 --> 00:08:15.250
"Michiru Natsuko Reiko"
Then...

00:08:16.750 --> 00:08:18.160
Let's go with Minare.

00:08:19.250 --> 00:08:22.500
Mr. Mato! I'm gonna go home
to strangle my father right now!

00:08:22.500 --> 00:08:24.790
--Hey, calm down.
--A direct physical confrontation would be
more useful as content, right?

00:08:24.790 --> 00:08:27.120
This is the radio; it doesn't matter either way.

00:08:27.120 --> 00:08:30.250
Mizuho! My adorable assistant director!
Get me two seats on the Starlight Kushiro train.

00:08:30.250 --> 00:08:33.910
That's impossible! It's 1 AM right now,
and we air at 3:30 AM!

00:08:33.910 --> 00:08:35.250
The station's ticket windows are closed,

00:08:35.250 --> 00:08:37.080
and you can only reserve over
the phone four days in advance.

00:08:37.080 --> 00:08:38.290
Two round trip tickets cost 21,000 yen.

00:08:38.290 --> 00:08:40.330
We would need approval from
the accounting department, too.

00:08:40.330 --> 00:08:44.200
Nanba, you didn't have to say anything else
beyond "It's 1 AM right now."

00:08:44.200 --> 00:08:45.830
What's all this commotion this late at night?

00:08:45.830 --> 00:08:47.040
Oh? Hey Kureko.

00:08:47.040 --> 00:08:48.040
Good evening.

00:08:48.040 --> 00:08:50.620
Okay... Fine, that's it...

00:08:50.620 --> 00:08:52.830
Men are just trash.

00:08:52.830 --> 00:08:56.790
I said I wanted my program to be fluffy
like a towel, but no, I take that back!

00:08:56.790 --> 00:08:59.830
Women will be healed; men will be bashed!

00:08:59.830 --> 00:09:03.040
"Miss Koda's program is interesting,
but isn't it a bit... you know?"

00:09:03.040 --> 00:09:07.290
Even the staff at the station won't
want to talk about my program

00:09:07.290 --> 00:09:08.370
--Got it, give me 30 minutes.
--loaded with feminist concepts!

00:09:08.370 --> 00:09:10.500
--It's fine to have a clear
contrast in reputation!
--loaded with feminist concepts!

00:09:10.500 --> 00:09:13.370
If I don't focus on a target audience,
nobody will listen to me!

00:09:13.370 --> 00:09:16.700
Are you trying to promote
gender-equality with your program?

00:09:16.700 --> 00:09:20.080
No, nothing lukewarm like that. I'm envisioning
something more like being an Amazon warrior.

00:09:20.080 --> 00:09:23.290
I'll kill every man in Hokkaido and take back
the women's country like in former Kuromatsunai.

00:09:23.290 --> 00:09:25.290
"Hokkaido"
"Right around here!"
I'll kill every man in Hokkaido and take back
the women's country like in former Kuromatsunai.

00:09:25.620 --> 00:09:30.910
Who should we kill first? Manager,
Mitsuo, or Dad? Now choose, Mizuho!

00:09:30.910 --> 00:09:32.410
--What? You want me to choose?
--Hey.

00:09:32.410 --> 00:09:35.000
Out of the ten ideas you prepared,

00:09:35.000 --> 00:09:38.450
I wrote the script based on
the "respond sincerely to 20 inquiries

00:09:38.450 --> 00:09:41.290
about relationships while
facing a brown bear" one.

00:09:41.290 --> 00:09:43.410
"What? A brown bear?"
Drop the idea from earlier.

00:09:43.410 --> 00:09:46.950
"What? A brown bear?"
Of course there's no time for street interviews
so use effects to make it work.

00:09:46.950 --> 00:09:50.540
For that reason, I brought Komoto here for you.

00:09:51.370 --> 00:09:54.500
If you want it to sound real,
it'd be better if it were a recording.

00:09:54.500 --> 00:09:56.080
We should let Mastering know.

00:09:56.080 --> 00:09:58.700
They already know it's going to be recorded.

00:09:58.700 --> 00:10:00.700
They'll complain if we're too late though.

00:10:00.700 --> 00:10:02.160
Want me to write up a cue sheet?

00:10:02.160 --> 00:10:05.500
No thanks. If I have ten minutes,
I can fix things up and write one up myself.

00:10:05.500 --> 00:10:07.500
It's a 20-minute program
without songs or commercials,

00:10:07.500 --> 00:10:09.330
so it'll turn out fine one way or another.

00:10:09.330 --> 00:10:13.160
While we have Komoto here,
we could re-record the opening, too.

00:10:13.160 --> 00:10:17.160
See, Miss Minare?
Men can bring you great despair,

00:10:17.160 --> 00:10:19.700
but they can also save your butt, too, at times.

00:10:19.700 --> 00:10:21.120
Don't you agree?

00:10:22.250 --> 00:10:26.620
I would've much preferred sending
a more competent helper,

00:10:26.620 --> 00:10:28.790
but I couldn't manage to find anyone else.

00:10:28.790 --> 00:10:32.950
But after consulting with Mr. Takarada,
we managed to devise a plan

00:10:32.950 --> 00:10:35.000
that'll make the most of the circumstances.

00:10:35.000 --> 00:10:37.330
--Now, Makie. Your job here is done.

00:10:37.330 --> 00:10:38.330
--No.
--Now, Makie. Your job here is done.

00:10:38.330 --> 00:10:40.040
What?

00:10:40.040 --> 00:10:42.250
I'm not going home.

00:10:42.250 --> 00:10:47.540
Hey, hold on a minute.
You can't just decide things like that.

00:10:47.540 --> 00:10:52.410
Mr. Takarada, you seem like you want to go back
to work, but you're obviously not ready yet.

00:10:52.410 --> 00:10:56.000
And anyway, your sister is
very helpful as a staff member.

00:10:56.000 --> 00:11:01.700
I was planning on asking Manager to see
if we can keep her as a regular paid staff.

00:11:01.700 --> 00:11:05.080
Nakahara, there's no need
to worry about staffing.

00:11:05.080 --> 00:11:09.040
When I spoke to the guy from Ceylon Shokai,
he said he'll let us use some of his staff.

00:11:09.040 --> 00:11:11.120
You demon! Read the air!

00:11:11.120 --> 00:11:15.620
Speaking of... What happened to the part-timer
who was hospitalized with you?

00:11:17.540 --> 00:11:21.830
Oh, it was so unfortunate
what happened to him...

00:11:21.830 --> 00:11:25.250
What? What do you mean? Did he--?!

00:11:25.250 --> 00:11:29.370
While we were hospitalized, he stole
morphine from the medicine vault

00:11:29.370 --> 00:11:32.580
and sold it to a drug dealer
who visited as a guest.

00:11:32.580 --> 00:11:35.250
He was taken away by the Hokkaido Police.

00:11:35.250 --> 00:11:40.080
That's crazy that he had an in
with the black market like that.

00:11:40.080 --> 00:11:46.790
He was a pure young man who wouldn't complain
when I would touch his butt! It's tragic...

00:11:48.370 --> 00:11:52.870
Corruption closely resembles...
the light of a rainbow!

00:11:52.870 --> 00:11:55.500
Manager, you love Yuming, don't you?

00:11:55.500 --> 00:12:00.450
Makie, I heard you were staying
at Voyager while helping out.

00:12:00.450 --> 00:12:03.790
So where were you about to go?

00:12:03.790 --> 00:12:05.620
To a friend's house...

00:12:05.620 --> 00:12:08.120
What... What friend?

00:12:08.120 --> 00:12:12.250
Even so, I never permitted you
to go out at night.

00:12:12.250 --> 00:12:16.410
What a line... Where are we?
Bangkok right after the coup?

00:12:17.870 --> 00:12:19.830
Mr. Tachibana...

00:12:19.830 --> 00:12:21.620
Miss Makie...

00:12:21.620 --> 00:12:24.830
She was going to come stay at my place tonight.

00:12:24.830 --> 00:12:27.040
Huh? What do you mean?

00:12:28.000 --> 00:12:29.870
Mr. Nakahara...

00:12:29.870 --> 00:12:35.830
While I am grateful for your kindness, we can't
spoil Makie like that. I appreciate the thought.

00:12:35.830 --> 00:12:40.040
Well, actually. She was staying
at my place this whole time.

00:12:40.040 --> 00:12:43.120
We weren't paying her, so we couldn't just
have her responsible for the restaurant

00:12:43.120 --> 00:12:45.000
while staying there... Right?

00:12:45.000 --> 00:12:48.000
And of course, she wasn't alone
with me. My sister and her--

00:13:02.580 --> 00:13:05.410
Stop it Brother! What are you doing?!

00:13:09.910 --> 00:13:11.330
Wh-What have I done?

00:13:11.330 --> 00:13:13.370
Mr. Nakahara, are you okay? Mr. Nakahara!

00:13:13.370 --> 00:13:15.580
What have I done?!

00:13:17.080 --> 00:13:19.160
I'm terribly sorry for causing you
trouble over and over again!

00:13:19.160 --> 00:13:19.750
Huh?

00:13:19.750 --> 00:13:22.870
When you've been taking care
of my sister all this time!

00:13:22.870 --> 00:13:24.660
Oh, it's fine...

00:13:24.660 --> 00:13:27.200
It was the way I said it, too.

00:13:27.200 --> 00:13:34.200
Whenever I lose my head over my sister,
I always lose my consciousness temporarily.

00:13:34.200 --> 00:13:38.290
Back in junior high, when I went to confront
a bully bothering Makie at his house,

00:13:38.290 --> 00:13:41.200
I lost consciousness at his doorstep...

00:13:42.200 --> 00:13:44.750
By the time I got it back,
the bully and his mother

00:13:44.750 --> 00:13:47.870
were wrapped in a bamboo mat
and almost drowned in the dam.

00:13:47.870 --> 00:13:50.790
I know I'm at fault for putting it that way...

00:13:50.790 --> 00:13:54.000
But even so, you should get
that checked out by a doctor...

00:13:54.000 --> 00:13:57.450
Come on, Brother! We're already
causing them so much trouble.

00:13:57.450 --> 00:13:59.580
--S-Sorry...
--Please stop. I'm begging you.

00:13:59.580 --> 00:14:02.250
Huh? Who are you calling?

00:14:03.870 --> 00:14:06.160
Oh, hey, do you have a minute?

00:14:06.160 --> 00:14:09.000
No, I'm still at the restaurant.

00:14:09.000 --> 00:14:12.120
But Miss Tachibana's brother is here right now.

00:14:12.120 --> 00:14:17.290
Yeah, and he said he wants
to talk to you. So, here he is.

00:14:17.290 --> 00:14:18.200
Here.

00:14:19.200 --> 00:14:20.080
Hello?

00:14:20.080 --> 00:14:22.910
Hello, it's very nice to meet you.

00:14:22.910 --> 00:14:25.790
This is Chuya Nakahara's sister.

00:14:27.250 --> 00:14:31.620
Um... I'm sorry for all the troubles
Makie has caused you...

00:14:31.620 --> 00:14:33.830
Speaking of causing trouble!

00:14:33.830 --> 00:14:39.500
I'm the one who barged into my younger brother's
place with my son, abandoning my husband!

00:14:39.500 --> 00:14:42.250
So it's actually been so helpful
having your sister around.

00:14:42.250 --> 00:14:45.410
Whenever I have her watch him
for even just a second,

00:14:45.410 --> 00:14:48.830
you wouldn't believe how attentive she is!

00:14:48.830 --> 00:14:51.700
Miss Makie would make a lovely wife.

00:14:51.700 --> 00:14:55.200
Is that so? I appreciate your kind words.

00:14:55.200 --> 00:14:57.450
But still, before she causes
any further trouble--

00:14:57.450 --> 00:15:00.700
Please, it's really not that big of a deal.

00:15:00.700 --> 00:15:03.540
Oh that reminds me of when we went
to the store together last time.

00:15:03.540 --> 00:15:07.450
A kid knocked over all these products
in front of us and started crying so loudly.

00:15:07.450 --> 00:15:09.040
--But the kid's mother was completely ignoring
him. That got me so bad, I wanted to--

00:15:09.040 --> 00:15:11.080
--I'm passing the phone back to your brother...
--But the kid's mother was completely ignoring
him. That got me so bad, I wanted to--

00:15:12.330 --> 00:15:18.250
Don't underestimate the gossip capacity of
a stay-at-home wife who's left alone all day.

00:15:18.250 --> 00:15:19.870
You really saved us all.

00:15:19.870 --> 00:15:23.660
I saw her brother's miasma
evaporate in front of me.

00:15:23.660 --> 00:15:31.250
But I strongly agree with my brother that I
should leave here as soon as possible.

00:15:31.250 --> 00:15:36.910
But if possible, I'd like to continue
working at the restaurant

00:15:36.910 --> 00:15:39.950
alongside Mr. Nakahara in the kitchen...

00:15:39.950 --> 00:15:43.750
So earlier, when you stood up for me...

00:15:43.750 --> 00:15:46.450
Um... It made me really happy.

00:15:46.450 --> 00:15:48.660
Well, yeah. Since you're part of the team now.

00:15:48.660 --> 00:15:52.250
Men like you are the toxic type.
Don't you get it?!

00:15:52.250 --> 00:15:55.330
Well, you say that you want to leave here...

00:15:55.330 --> 00:15:56.700
Will you go back home?

00:15:56.700 --> 00:15:59.910
I do not want to go back home
to my brother anymore.

00:15:59.910 --> 00:16:06.540
Miss Meiko asked me what it was
my brother ultimately wants for me.

00:16:06.540 --> 00:16:09.750
My brother wants me to stay ignorant
of the ways of the world.

00:16:09.750 --> 00:16:15.620
He wants me to catch a city banker or
government worker at a matchmaking party

00:16:15.620 --> 00:16:20.500
so I can become a stay-at-home wife
who doesn't have to worry about anything.

00:16:20.500 --> 00:16:23.540
That's what he seriously thinks is best for me.

00:16:23.540 --> 00:16:27.660
Well I'm sure you'd be popular at
a matchmaking party, Miss Tachibana.

00:16:27.660 --> 00:16:30.790
I didn't think your brother
would allow you to go to those things.

00:16:30.790 --> 00:16:39.830
When I heard my brother mention "marriage,"
I realized I was at a point of no return.

00:16:39.830 --> 00:16:41.540
Yes...

00:16:41.540 --> 00:16:44.540
When I look back on it, I've never
been assertive to my brother

00:16:44.540 --> 00:16:52.160
about what I want to be
or how I want to live in the future.

00:16:52.160 --> 00:16:53.910
I was too scared.

00:16:53.910 --> 00:17:00.040
Basically, your brother believes that you don't
have the ability to live your own life.

00:17:00.040 --> 00:17:05.290
Well then I get how he could
get overprotective to a point.

00:17:05.290 --> 00:17:08.160
Why don't you mention that you want
to be a curry restaurant owner's wife?

00:17:08.160 --> 00:17:09.290
Wife?

00:17:09.290 --> 00:17:15.000
But I only started working at the restaurant
because things just worked out that way.

00:17:15.000 --> 00:17:18.660
That's why I don't think
he'll believe that I'm serious.

00:17:18.660 --> 00:17:21.330
He'll assume it's just an excuse to escape.

00:17:21.330 --> 00:17:26.540
But, actually, I have something
in mind that I really want to do.

00:17:26.540 --> 00:17:30.080
I've been preparing for it steadily.

00:17:30.080 --> 00:17:35.450
And this is something I wouldn't have thought
of if it weren't for me working at Voyager.

00:17:35.450 --> 00:17:39.000
It all feels like fate to me.

00:17:39.000 --> 00:17:44.580
It's time for Minare Koda's Wave, Listen to Me!

00:17:44.580 --> 00:17:47.620
All right! The current time is 3:30 AM.

00:17:47.620 --> 00:17:51.160
People, what do you want this late at night?

00:17:51.160 --> 00:17:54.250
This is Minare Koda in charge of
bringing you live noise from Sapporo.

00:17:54.250 --> 00:17:58.540
There you go. That was
the innocuous intro you all wanted.

00:17:58.540 --> 00:18:01.540
But I must confess right now...

00:18:01.540 --> 00:18:05.450
I'm... Being glared at...

00:18:05.450 --> 00:18:06.370
...by a brown bear.

00:18:06.370 --> 00:18:07.620
"*The photo is just an image."

00:18:07.750 --> 00:18:11.620
No, I'm not at a zoo. I'm in the mountains!

00:18:11.620 --> 00:18:12.790
By a stream!

00:18:12.790 --> 00:18:15.790
By a stream that looks about 15 meters wide.

00:18:15.790 --> 00:18:20.540
By the way, I forgot to mention that we're
presenting live from Mt. Sapporo tonight.

00:18:21.120 --> 00:18:26.120
"*It all ties together with
the beginning of episode 1."

00:18:26.410 --> 00:18:30.160
Keep yourself alive!

00:18:35.830 --> 00:18:38.290
Just be true to yourself!

00:18:38.290 --> 00:18:41.200
Even if you fall all the way to the bottom,

00:18:41.200 --> 00:18:46.370
if you live your life earnestly,
someone will help you no matter what.

00:18:46.370 --> 00:18:49.700
That's because... people are...

00:18:49.700 --> 00:18:53.500
...mirrors for each other...

00:18:53.500 --> 00:18:54.870
It happens every time...

00:18:54.870 --> 00:18:59.790
You project your own feelings to
the listeners during the ad-lib portion.

00:18:59.790 --> 00:19:02.910
Ah, well anyway, good job for now.

00:19:02.910 --> 00:19:07.370
So why am I doing this again...?

00:19:07.410 --> 00:19:09.410
"Data is being transferred now..."

00:19:12.080 --> 00:19:13.790
Miss Minare, that was impressive.

00:19:13.790 --> 00:19:15.790
Ah, thanks...

00:19:17.200 --> 00:19:19.080
--Ah, Mr. Kureko.
--Huh?

00:19:19.080 --> 00:19:21.370
Did something good happen?

00:19:21.370 --> 00:19:23.910
Did the hemorrhoid you suffered
a long time from heal up or something?

00:19:23.910 --> 00:19:25.000
What?

00:19:25.000 --> 00:19:30.160
You wrote a script without even being asked to.

00:19:30.160 --> 00:19:32.700
This one was the easiest to read.

00:19:32.700 --> 00:19:35.540
"Stare..."
It was a well-rounded script.

00:19:35.540 --> 00:19:38.790
I'm kept here to deal
with situations like these.

00:19:38.790 --> 00:19:41.120
Glad you liked it.

00:19:41.120 --> 00:19:43.040
It's a parting gift.

00:19:43.040 --> 00:19:44.000
Huh?

00:19:49.000 --> 00:19:52.500
Sorry to put you through that
when you were just about to leave.

00:19:52.500 --> 00:19:55.120
Tell that to Komoto.

00:19:55.120 --> 00:19:58.120
I just happened to stop by the booth.

00:19:59.750 --> 00:20:02.250
That thing I mentioned to you before...

00:20:02.250 --> 00:20:03.250
It's moving forward.

00:20:03.250 --> 00:20:07.830
What? You mean...
the Ranzo Arakawa Prize?

00:20:07.830 --> 00:20:08.870
Yeah.

00:20:08.870 --> 00:20:11.120
I see...

00:20:11.120 --> 00:20:15.290
So the time has come for you to move on...

00:20:22.410 --> 00:20:23.790
Hey.

00:20:25.620 --> 00:20:28.330
Come sit here and look as this.

00:20:31.660 --> 00:20:35.120
Turns out there are dirty jokes
in the Ainu language.

00:20:37.120 --> 00:20:41.500
Well, what else can people do while they're
trapped by snow during winter in Hokkaido?

00:20:43.750 --> 00:20:46.000
"Are you studying Ainu?"

00:20:47.330 --> 00:20:52.500
My dad was given these presentation materials
from someone at the radio station.

00:20:53.620 --> 00:20:54.500
It's great!

00:20:54.500 --> 00:20:57.790
When there's an abundance of jokes,
that's proof that the culture's maturing!

00:20:57.790 --> 00:21:00.540
Comedy is so crucial!

00:21:00.540 --> 00:21:03.950
The radio I want to do is going to be funny.

00:21:05.290 --> 00:21:08.120
When I saw Monty Python in London,

00:21:08.120 --> 00:21:11.580
it was cool and I appreciated the black humor,
but that's not the comedy I aim for.

00:21:14.000 --> 00:21:15.950
Instead of making fun of others,

00:21:15.950 --> 00:21:19.040
it's much more precious when you can
make others laugh by embarrassing yourself.

00:21:20.700 --> 00:21:21.910
If I ever have a kid,

00:21:21.910 --> 00:21:24.870
I might name it this.

00:21:28.040 --> 00:21:31.500
"MINA RE "TO MAKE LAUGH""
Mina... re...

00:21:34.700 --> 00:21:36.330
Have a good night!

00:21:36.330 --> 00:21:37.540
Good night.

00:21:41.410 --> 00:21:44.500
Oh?

00:21:44.500 --> 00:21:46.330
I got a text. You can go ahead.

00:21:46.330 --> 00:21:49.330
Then I'll be setting up for a celebration!

00:21:49.330 --> 00:21:51.370
Who can it be this late at night?

00:21:51.660 --> 00:21:52.580
"Mitsuo"

00:21:52.580 --> 00:21:53.410
"Inbox
Hey
4:44  Mitsuo"

00:21:53.410 --> 00:21:55.160
"Wanna meet up? By the way,
I heard you on the radio."

00:21:57.160 --> 00:21:58.910
"I will shoot him to death!"

00:23:28.950 --> 00:23:30.160
"Next episode"

00:23:30.160 --> 00:23:30.700
"Next episode"
Hey, Mina! Mina!

00:23:30.700 --> 00:23:31.870
"Preview"
Hey, Mina! Mina!

00:23:31.870 --> 00:23:34.290
"Preview"
How could he not change at all?

00:23:34.290 --> 00:23:36.870
--I have something to give you right now.
--What?

00:23:36.870 --> 00:23:38.910
It's only 250,000 yen. Sorry!

00:23:38.910 --> 00:23:41.040
I promise I'll pay you back
completely by the end of the year.

00:23:41.040 --> 00:23:44.080
Um, wait... Did you really
come see me to pay me back?

00:23:44.080 --> 00:23:47.950
There aren't any girls out there
better than you, Mina.

00:23:47.950 --> 00:23:49.040
Do you wanna come over?

00:23:49.040 --> 00:23:49.870
What?!

00:23:49.870 --> 00:23:52.660
Oh, I love your thighs, Mina.

00:23:52.660 --> 00:23:54.290
What's gonna happen to me?!

00:23:54.290 --> 00:23:57.580
Next on <i>Wave, Listen to Me!:</i>
"I Won't Believe You."

00:23:58.950 --> 00:24:01.870
"Illustrated by Hiroaki Samura"
"See you next time!"
